{% doc %}
  Product block `video` (docs/WAVE1-CONTRACTS.md §1), rendered by snippets/anvil-product-block.liquid with the
  fixed arguments product, block, section, form_id and current_variant; it reads block and section (the gallery width).

  A Shopify-hosted video (video_tag) or a YouTube/Vimeo link (click-to-load facade, nothing loads before the tap)
  through snippets/anvil-media. Autoplay applies to Shopify videos only: anvil-core.js plays them muted while in
  view and only when the shopper allows motion; their controls stay visible so they can always be paused. A
  click-to-play Shopify video can start without sound ("muted"); autoplay always starts muted. The poster
  image covers a YouTube/Vimeo facade; the title names the video for screen readers. Placeholder when empty.
  Styles: assets/anvil-pb-content.css (media box styles live in assets/anvil-base.css).

  No LiquidDoc parameter tags on purpose: the dispatcher always passes all five arguments, and Theme Check
  reports either the unused ones here (UnusedDocParam) or the undeclared ones at the call site
  (UnrecognizedRenderSnippetArguments).
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings
  assign video_title = s.title | strip
  # The buy column is what the gallery leaves from 750 px (anvil-product.css), 45 % by default.
  assign col_pct = 100 | minus: section.settings.layout_gallery_width
  if col_pct < 20 or col_pct > 80
    assign col_pct = 45
  endif
  assign poster_sizes = '(min-width: 750px) ' | append: col_pct | append: 'vw, 100vw'
-%}
{{ 'anvil-pb-content.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<div class="av-pb-video" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- render 'anvil-media',
    video: s.video,
    video_url: s.video_url,
    image: s.poster,
    ratio: s.image_ratio,
    widths: '300, 450, 600, 800, 1100',
    sizes: poster_sizes,
    alt: video_title,
    autoplay: s.video_autoplay,
    muted: s.muted,
    loop: s.loop,
    placeholder: 'lifestyle-1',
    class: 'av-pb-video__media'
  -%}
</div>
